-- 01: operations carry no capabilities; the policy is orthogonal; the grade
--     is inferred.
--
-- POC for OCP-0007 (capability-graded effects). NOT compilable today.
--
-- The library and its interpretations declare only OPERATIONS. Capabilities
-- are NOT a library concern — they are a separate, orthogonal policy axis owned
-- by the deployment. The same operation, under the same interpretation, may
-- carry different capability policies in different deployments.

-- The operation: plain Eff, no capability annotation anywhere.
signature putLine : Eff (String Utf8) Unit

-- The capability policy: a SEPARATE artifact (a deployment choice), independent
-- of which interpretation actually provides `putLine`.
require putLine : {Console}

-- What the compiler INFERS for code that uses the op. This grade is the truth,
-- computed bottom-up — you do not write it (D007: a signature only verifies,
-- it never changes meaning). It is mostly something the compiler SHOWS you.
--
--   greet : (String Utf8) →[{Console}] Unit
greet : Eff (String Utf8) Unit
greet = putLine

-- `main` is the root capability holder; here the {Console} requirement is
-- discharged by the root grant (see 04 for grant/attenuate).
main : IO Unit
main = greet "Hello for Once"
